[*What would a person be like if they lived alone in a spaceship for 50 years?]

After 50 years of social isolation, even with spiritual companionship such as books and entertainment, a person would become alienated:

[role dddblue [*Sensory deprivation effect:]] The monotonous environment leads to a sense of confusion about time, the illusion of time dilation/compression, and a scattered attention.

[role dddblue [*Emotional dullness and alexithymia:]] With no one to empathize with for a long time, one will gradually lose the ability to recognize and express complex emotions.

[role dddblue [*Hallucinations and paranoia:]] When isolated for too long, it is common to imagine sounds, form a strong projective attachment to objects, and treat objects as "people" or even "family members".

[role dddblue [*Depersonalization and weakened sense of reality:]] One may not be able to distinguish between true and false memories, or start to regard past life on Earth as a "dream".

[role dddblue [*Cognitive rigidity or reconstruction:]] Some people develop an extreme philosophical or religious inner world, while others fall into depressive stupor.

[role dddred [*Result:]] There is a very high probability of severe loning-related mental disorders occurring. A few "adaptors" will become highly introspective but emotionally different from the average person.

